Z||000000||My7Fieros||10-07-2000||10:13 PM||||Good God its always something! Well now Ive got a gimpy headlight. I actually rebuilt these lights not to long ago..but this is a diff problem. The drivers side headlight comes up SOMETIMES....its not the usual "motor spins but light dosnt come up" problem, I fixed that with the rebuild. Now sometimes (more times than not) when I turn on the lights, only the pass side works...nothing happens on the drivers side. Motor dosnt spin, nothing. I can flick them on and off several times, and it'll eventually go up. Could this be a relay problem? If so, where in the he11 is the relay? <BR>Ogre, I'll pay you to move to Memphis!<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-07-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||Seanh||10-07-2000||11:42 PM||||What year Fiero is it? If it an 87+ you might have a bad contoller. If it is 86-, yes, it is probally a relay problem, or you might have some corroded contacts somwhere in the wiring. I would start with relays, thats probally what it is.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
