Z||000003||862M4inCA||10-08-2000||03:04 AM||||I know this pro'll wouldn't apply to the 87-88 systems, but I've noticed on mine (86)that my drivers side motor occasionally "sticks" and I have to get out, open the front hood, and give the manual knob a little help and the light comes right up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||10-08-2000||08:49 AM||||That relay on the '87 & '88 models is located behind the drivers side fender. Th gain access to it loosen the fender well on the front side, remove as many screws as necessary to gain access. It loos like a 5x5 square about a 1/2" thick on the edges, and maybe 1 1/4" thick in the middle with a 7 (?) wire connector.<BR>Double check grounds and +12 volts at harness, may be dirty contacts inside motor.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||10-08-2000||12:30 PM||||It posible but I doubt the control box is an issue. maybe a loose connector or the motor needs to be taken apart again.<P>The motor could be worn out. shot brushes that sort of thing. Or something is jammed in there so the controler shuts it off, which is exactly what the controller should do.<P>could be you got lubricant on the brushes or armature. lube there usually burns up after awhile and keeps the brushes from making contact on the armature.||||reg||1
